    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0636" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg524"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Taft to Her Majesty Queen
                    Alexandra.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The White House</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-05-06"><hi rendition="#italic">May 6,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>On the sad occasion of the death of King Edward I offer to Your Majesty and to
                    your son, his illustrious successor, the most profound sympathy of the people
                    and of the Government of the United States whose hearts go out to their British
                    kinsmen in this, their national bereavement. To this I add the expression to
                    Your Majesty and to the new King of my own personal sympathy and of my
                    appreciation of those high qualities which made the life of the late King so
                    potent an influence toward peace and justice among the nations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Taft.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
